From ab1ae42a01333388967589b6dc1e91e695914cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gx-bangsong <146644201+gx-bangsong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:23:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] numberinfo: keep the trunk prefix when normalizing +86
 landlines

NumberNormalizer stripped +86 and returned the bare national number, so
"+86 10 1234 5678" became "1012345678" while the same number dialed
domestically is "01012345678". PREFIX rules such as "010" never matched
landlines that Telecom delivers in E.164 form, cache rows were split
between the two forms, and web sources were queried with a wrong number.

- +86 landlines (10/2X + 8 digits, 3XX-9XX + 7-8 digits) regain the "0";
  mobiles, 400/800 and short service numbers are unchanged
- "+86 (0)10 ..." mis-format no longer doubles the zero
- "00" is treated as the international access prefix ("0044" == "+44")
- full-width digits / plus sign from CJK input methods are accepted
- new normalizePrefix() for rule prefixes; a bare "+86" yields null
  instead of an empty prefix that would match every number
---
