From 730bb6c2742edc8593dec0286675ea597da5f241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gx-bangsong <146644201+gx-bangsong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:23:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] callscreening: store and match rule values in canonical
 form

Rule values were saved verbatim while incoming numbers are normalized,
so a blacklist entry pasted as "+86 138 0013 8000" (or "138-0013-8000")
could never match the incoming "13800138000".

RuleValues.normalize() defines the canonical value per rule type and is
applied when saving from the editor (invalid values are rejected inline),
when importing JSON (unusable rows are skipped and counted), and again in
the decision engine so rows written by earlier builds keep working
without a database migration.
