From c7ffc53adda7a1c4f2fd43d7b6a4b8d025d26d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gx-bangsong <146644201+gx-bangsong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:23:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] numberinfo: lock online refreshes per number instead of
 globally

A single repository-wide Mutex serialized online lookups for all
numbers, so a slow in-call refresh of one number could consume the
screening budget of the next incoming call from another number.

Refreshes now lock per number (KeyedMutex, entries dropped when idle).
query() reads the cache after the online phase, so a caller that waited
for a concurrent refresh of the same number gets its results instead of
an empty online phase.
